# {{projectName}}

This is a generated TinyGres TypeScript/Vite starter.

- Work in `client/` and run `npm run dev` there.
- TinyGres owns its {{#if usesOpfs}}OPFS-backed{{else}}in-memory{{/if}} data and
  query engine inside a dedicated Worker.
{{#if isSupabase}}
- The built-in read-only Supabase source owns snapshots and incoming changes for
  `public.tinygres_posts`; do not call `replaceTable` or `applyBatch` from UI
  code and do not invent an upstream-write path.
- Keep the table mapping, `supabase.sql`, rendered query, RLS policy, replica
  identity, and Realtime publication configuration aligned.
- Browser configuration belongs in ignored `client/.env.local`. Keep only
  placeholders in `.env.example`, and never expose a secret or service-role key.
- Preserve immediate cached rendering after `ready()`, invalidation-driven
  re-querying, explicit sync state, `whenSynced()`, and client cleanup.
{{else}}
- Treat `replaceTable` and `applyBatch` as read-only source integration seams,
  not as local application mutation APIs.
{{#if usesOpfs}}
- Preserve the stable `{{storageName}}` OPFS name and do not replace restored
  rows with the demo seed on reload.
{{/if}}
{{/if}}
- Preserve parameterized SQL and the explicit table schema.
- Validate changes with `npm run build`.
